Z||000000||Oreif||07-11-2000||07:13 PM||||I just got a flyer from the Fiero Store. The are now offering an 84-87 Fiero brake upgrade for the front brakes. It uses bigger vented rotors, Bigger calipers (piston is 5mm bigger) Hubs, Pads, caliper mounting plates, bearings, and all associated hardware for $289.00 plus for another $49.00 you can get a big bore master cylinder.<BR>The picture of the kit looks like everything is there. It says it is a complete bolt-on kit. I am thinking about getting it. Any opinions on it?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||07-11-2000||07:23 PM||||Wow, if it's that simple.. they should call it an "easy bake"!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Does it come with a special attachment for putting little cookies and cakes above it?<BR>hehehehe..<P>seriously though, for $300... if it is a direct bolt on and has substantial performance increases over the GA conversion.. it might not be too bad.. sure beats $1,000 from pisa or ryane...<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||10
